harness/node_modules/

# Repeat-run row-level artifacts (separate-process determinism).
#
# `scripts/reproduce.sh` runs Phase B three times in three separate processes
# (main, det1, det2). The det1/det2 row-level files come out byte-identical to
# the main run apart from their `run_tag`, so committing them adds ~4 MB of
# duplication to a repository whose entire packed history is smaller than that.
#
# The evidence they carry is their decision and raw-score DIGESTS, and those are
# retained in results/determinism-summary.json, which is committed. compare_runs.js
# refuses to regenerate that summary into a weaker verdict when the row-level runs
# are absent, so dropping these files cannot silently erase the claim.
#
# Row-level predictions for the `main` run on every architecture ARE committed:
# they are the substrate for re-scoring and for the cross-architecture audit.
results/predictions/*.det[0-9].json
results/results.det[0-9].json
